<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19544" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gestĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		gero. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A managing</i>, <i>doing</i>, <i>performing</i> (perh. only in the foll. passages; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syn.: actio, administratio): in gestione autem
					negotii, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 26, 38</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 12,
			39</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A behaving</i>, <i>acting</i> in any
			manner, <i><span class="en">Dig. 11, 7, 14, §
		8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
